let gaussianBlurParamsBuffer = device.makeBuffer(bytes: &gaussianBlurParams, length: MemoryLayout<GaussianBlurParams>.size, options: [])

commandEncoder.setComputePipelineState(gaussianBlurFunction)
commandEncoder.setTexture(texture, slot: 0)
commandEncoder.setTexture(destinationTexture, slot: 1)
commandEncoder.setBuffer(gaussianBlurParamsBuffer, offset: 0, index: 0)
```

Finally, you can dispatch the compute kernel on the GPU:

```
let threadExecutionWidth = 8
let threadGroupsPerGridX = (textureWidth + threadExecutionWidth - 1) / threadExecutionWidth
let threadgroups = MTLSize(width: threadGroupsPerGridX, height: textureHeight, depth: 1)
commandEncoder.dispatchThreadgroups(threadgroups, threadsPerThreadgroup: MTLSize(width: threadExecutionWidth, height: 1, depth: 1))
```

This kernel function performs a 2D Gaussian blur by sampling neighboring pixels with a Gaussian distribution and computing a weighted sum of the colors. The radius and standard deviation of the Gaussian distribution can be specified with the `radius` and `sigma` parameters, respectively. The `texel_size` parameter specifies the size of a single texel in the input and output textures.

