The `waitfor` function will pause the execution of the script until the figure specified as its argument is closed. In this case, we are using `gcf` to specify the current figure, so the script will wait for the user to close the current figure before continuing.

If you want to wait for all figures to be closed, rather than just the current figure, you can use the `gcf` function in a loop to wait for each figure to be closed, like this:
```
% Open some figures
figure;
plot(1:10);
figure;
plot(10:-1:1);

% Wait for all figures to be closed
figures = gcf;
while ~isempty(figures)
    waitfor(figures(1));
    figures = gcf;
end

% The script will continue here after all figures have been closed
disp('All figures have been closed');
```
This will wait for the first figure to be closed, then wait for the next figure to be closed, and so on, until all figures have been closed.

