To create a more realistic 3D illusion, you would need to use more advanced techniques such as 3D transforms and projections. Unfortunately, SVG doesn't support 3D transforms directly, so you would need to use a library or framework that provides this functionality.

One such library is three.js, which is a popular JavaScript library for creating 3D graphics in the browser. You could use three.js to create a 3D model of an impossible triangle and then render it inside an SVG using a canvas element.

